// Two decks meeting at one module — the shape a single chain cannot express, because a chain
// carries ONE signal.
//
// `deckA` FLOWS into the crossfade: a bare destination is the flow, so the crossfade continues
// deckA's run as a step. `deckB` names a PORT, `#b`, so it lands on the module's second input
// without claiming it as its own next step — which is what stops deckB from swallowing the
// module and leaving its real input unnoticed.
//
// The decks are in `modules:` like everything else: a lane is a module too, and a run is named
// after the lane that starts it (packages/song/docs/trackModules.md).
//
// There is no chain called `crossfade`: it has one flow feeder, so it is a step inside deckA's
// run rather than a meeting point. See packages/song/docs/ports.md.

// `MIX` is the mixer's sum and `OUT` is the interface; the run between them is the MASTER
// CHAIN, and `OUT` carries the song's output level as its `Volume`. Name a module on that
// line and it processes the blend rather than either deck.

modules({
  deckA: ["@workspace/audio/crossfade"],
  deckB: ["@workspace/audio/crossfade#b"],
  "@workspace/audio/crossfade": ["MIX"],
  MIX: ["OUT"],
})

// deckB's mute. See nodes/deckB.yaml for why it is not optional.
bypassed(["deckB"])
